WEBVTT

01:32.467 --> 01:33.676
Mr. Shishiba?

01:34.219 --> 01:35.136
What is it?

01:36.304 --> 01:39.224
Now I understand
what you were saying the other day.

01:39.849 --> 01:40.724
Huh?

01:40.725 --> 01:43.644
It gets on your nerves
when someone wrecks your home.

01:43.645 --> 01:45.104
I told you so.

01:45.939 --> 01:49.233
Though I must say,
this is much worse than a simple "wreck."

01:49.234 --> 01:52.153
40 percent of the Kanto Branch
has been destroyed,

01:52.737 --> 01:55.030
and the JAA stocks took a sharp fall.

01:55.031 --> 01:58.701
I heard many clients
are cancelling hit requests, too.

01:59.327 --> 02:01.371
They've done some serious damage.

02:02.122 --> 02:02.955
Wait a minute.

02:02.956 --> 02:04.790
What about our annual bonus?

02:04.791 --> 02:06.792
I wouldn't expect much.

02:06.793 --> 02:08.585
It's over...

02:08.586 --> 02:09.796
You're overreacting.

02:10.839 --> 02:15.884
Upper management has decided
to revise some of the JAA regulations.

02:15.885 --> 02:17.719
We lost a lot of people,

02:17.720 --> 02:20.223
so they'll have to find replacements, too.

02:23.309 --> 02:24.434
Are you listening?

02:24.435 --> 02:26.020
Anyway,

02:26.604 --> 02:28.939
I suppose we'll need to gather the others

02:28.940 --> 02:31.276
and have them come back soon.

02:31.860 --> 02:33.694
The other Order members?

02:33.695 --> 02:34.654
That's right.

02:35.321 --> 02:37.782
I wonder what Kanaguri's been up to?

02:38.366 --> 02:40.118
I don't like him.

02:40.618 --> 02:42.162
Come on now, play nice.

02:58.970 --> 03:00.930
The nerve suture is complete.

03:01.764 --> 03:05.684
Your nerve fibers will recover slowly,
like a sprouting plant.

03:05.685 --> 03:08.771
It will take a while
before you can feel your fingertips.

03:09.272 --> 03:12.775
Try not to move it much
until the blood flow stabilizes.

03:13.359 --> 03:16.070
Awesome. It's really connected.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.655
Thanks, Mr. Kashima.

03:18.656 --> 03:21.326
You should be thanking
the person who cut it off.

03:21.868 --> 03:26.164
The cut was so clean that
the muscle tissue hardly had any damage.

03:26.873 --> 03:28.333
Who was this person?

03:28.875 --> 03:31.669
Who could come this close
to defeating you?

03:38.843 --> 03:40.386
Don't let it bother you, Gaku.

03:41.554 --> 03:46.434
You're probably the first person ever
to survive a battle against Mr. Takamura.

03:46.976 --> 03:47.810
Boss.

03:50.647 --> 03:53.233
Good to see your arm's back together.

03:53.858 --> 03:55.859
He says he won't fix my ear, though.

03:55.860 --> 03:58.488
Even I have my limits!

04:02.408 --> 04:04.494
You seem rather tired.

04:05.370 --> 04:06.829
Yeah, I'm exhausted.

04:08.289 --> 04:10.375
The attack on the JAA was a failure.

04:10.875 --> 04:12.835
I didn't expect to see Mr. Takamura.

04:14.254 --> 04:17.173
At the end, Uda saved the day.

04:18.383 --> 04:21.094
So, what's the deal with that old dude?

04:22.720 --> 04:24.013
I don't know.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.350
<i>How long he's been in The Order,</i>

04:27.850 --> 04:30.603
<i>what his relationship is to the JAA,</i>

04:31.187 --> 04:34.023
<i>or even what he's thinking... No one knows.</i>

04:34.607 --> 04:38.319
<i>Aside from his incredible strength,
Mr. Takamura is a complete mystery.</i>

04:39.362 --> 04:42.823
Personally, I sometimes wonder
whether he's something

04:42.824 --> 04:44.700
like a ghost, or a monster.

04:44.701 --> 04:48.454
Perhaps, he's a being
manifested out of peoples' imaginations.

04:49.580 --> 04:52.207
The idea that if everyone
in the world believes something,

04:52.208 --> 04:55.252
that "something" would become real?

04:55.253 --> 05:00.216
So he's like the culmination of bloodlust
gathered from all the assassins on earth?

05:00.758 --> 05:02.510
No wonder he's that strong.

05:04.262 --> 05:05.387
Perhaps, collectively,

05:05.388 --> 05:08.433
our minds have enough energy
to create a whole person.

05:09.392 --> 05:12.227
Well, that's enough
ghost stories for today.

05:12.228 --> 05:14.604
With someone that strong against us,

05:14.605 --> 05:16.983
things won't be as simple as we thought.

05:18.776 --> 05:20.486
<i>And there's Sakamoto, too.</i>

05:21.321 --> 05:25.074
<i>I did not expect to see you like this.</i>

05:26.701 --> 05:29.620
So, what do we do now?

05:30.246 --> 05:33.457
You wanna gather the others
and go on a Japan tour?

05:33.458 --> 05:35.960
There are lots of JAA branches, right?

05:37.962 --> 05:39.047
Oh, of course not.

05:39.672 --> 05:42.132
We won't be risking our chances like that.

05:42.133 --> 05:46.136
I'm sure the other branches will have
heightened their security measures.

05:46.137 --> 05:48.555
Now that Uda's gone,

05:48.556 --> 05:51.099
I suppose it's time we added more pawns.

05:51.100 --> 05:54.270
Gonna recruit from the JAA?

05:54.771 --> 05:55.604
No...

05:55.605 --> 05:58.274
I want pawns that are untainted.

05:59.067 --> 06:02.487
Blank canvases are easier to paint on.

06:03.780 --> 06:05.740
Preparations are already in place.

06:07.950 --> 06:09.534
By the way, Mr. Sakamoto,

06:09.535 --> 06:13.371
I'm happy to go to the JCC
to gather information on Slur,

06:13.372 --> 06:18.044
but to be honest,
I don't know much about the JCC.

06:18.586 --> 06:20.879
I got my license through an external exam.

06:20.880 --> 06:22.089
What?

06:22.090 --> 06:24.132
Do you mean you got your license

06:24.133 --> 06:25.717
without going to school?!

06:25.718 --> 06:27.511
Uh, well... Yeah.

06:27.512 --> 06:29.304
No way, that's crazy!

06:29.305 --> 06:31.765
- No wonder you're Taro's partner!
<i>- All fresh batches...</i>

06:31.766 --> 06:32.725
Right, Piisuke?

06:33.392 --> 06:36.020
The Floaters fixed everything
back to normal!

06:36.687 --> 06:38.856
<i>That idiot Nagumo must've made a mess.</i>

06:39.398 --> 06:41.358
You really are a genius!

06:41.359 --> 06:43.527
Come on, drop it already!

06:43.528 --> 06:46.571
JCC is that school for hit men, right?

06:46.572 --> 06:48.490
- Is this the one?
- Huh?

06:48.491 --> 06:49.407
A STRESS-FREE SCHOOL

06:49.408 --> 06:51.368
I didn't know they had a homepage.

06:51.369 --> 06:54.538
"JCC Incorporated Educational Institution,

06:54.539 --> 06:58.835
a boarding school with 35 instructors,
and a four-year program."

06:59.335 --> 07:02.755
"1,000 students with a
male to female ratio of eight to two."

07:03.297 --> 07:07.676
"Ten percent of the students
obtain their hit man licenses,

07:07.677 --> 07:12.390
and the other 90 percent
either quit or die during training."

07:13.391 --> 07:15.017
I'd never want to go here.

07:15.518 --> 07:17.352
Man, those were the days.

07:17.353 --> 07:19.312
Go to the page about annual events.

07:19.313 --> 07:23.150
Mr. Manager,
you graduated from the JCC, right?

07:23.151 --> 07:26.028
Can you go visit as an alum?

07:26.529 --> 07:30.116
No, the JCC doesn't let people
in its grounds that easily.

07:30.658 --> 07:32.159
Their security is very tight.

07:32.160 --> 07:34.537
It is? Then how are we going to--

07:36.747 --> 07:39.625
I found this as I was cleaning
the living room just now.

07:40.168 --> 07:43.004
Would you care to explain what this is?

07:44.589 --> 07:45.964
Taro, you'd better not be

07:45.965 --> 07:48.467
trying to raise Hana to be an assassin!

07:48.468 --> 07:49.509
No, ma'am.

07:49.510 --> 07:51.554
"JCC Transfer Exam"?

07:52.096 --> 07:54.890
"General Admissions Policy"?

07:54.891 --> 07:56.641
You don't mean...

07:56.642 --> 07:58.811
TRANSFERS WELCOME!
JOIN US, FUTURE HIT MEN!

08:00.104 --> 08:04.108
<i>Please make sure your seatbelt
is fastened securely around your waist.</i>

08:05.443 --> 08:08.946
<i>This flight will be arriving
at your destination in three hours.</i>

08:09.447 --> 08:12.658
<i>Feel free to ask a flight attendant
if you need any assistance.</i>

08:13.242 --> 08:15.619
We're going undercover as students?

08:15.620 --> 08:17.746
It's the safest, surest way.

08:17.747 --> 08:19.915
They'll notice just by our ages!

08:19.916 --> 08:21.416
No need to worry about that.

08:21.417 --> 08:22.835
Look around you.

08:25.296 --> 08:26.463
You're right.

08:26.464 --> 08:28.424
Everyone's older than I expected.

08:29.008 --> 08:31.510
The JCC has no age limit.

08:31.511 --> 08:35.222
This transfer exam
is especially difficult to pass.

08:35.223 --> 08:37.933
Some fail many times
and take it year after year.

08:37.934 --> 08:39.351
I didn't know.

08:39.352 --> 08:40.520
SALTED SEAWEED POTATO CHIPS

08:41.604 --> 08:44.857
But Mr. Sakamoto, you're an alum!
Won't they recognize you?

08:45.483 --> 08:46.900
I'll disguise myself.

08:46.901 --> 08:49.319
That's how you're gonna get past security?

08:49.320 --> 08:52.740
Just wearing a cap?
There's no way they won't notice!

08:53.366 --> 08:57.160
What's with all the yappin'?
Annoying newbies.

08:57.161 --> 08:59.037
They'll get killed soon anyway.

08:59.038 --> 09:01.915
<i>Wow, those two are really something.</i>

09:01.916 --> 09:04.126
<i>Aren't they nervous at all?</i>

09:05.795 --> 09:07.963
MAY YOU PASS THE EXAM

09:07.964 --> 09:10.049
<i>No, I need to stop doubting myself.</i>

09:10.633 --> 09:13.469
<i>I'm gonna be an assassin. I'm gonna do it.</i>

09:23.229 --> 09:25.356
I wonder what level we can expect

09:25.982 --> 09:29.819
from people who come
to take the JCC Transfer Exam?

09:30.361 --> 09:34.447
The Transfer Exam is much harder
than the General Admissions Exam.

09:34.448 --> 09:37.034
Many applicants
are already good enough to be pros.

09:37.868 --> 09:39.411
Keep your guard up.

09:39.412 --> 09:40.579
Yes, sir.

09:40.580 --> 09:43.248
Why are those two
wolfing down food before the exam?

09:43.249 --> 09:44.249
He ate so many.

09:44.250 --> 09:45.500
It's not an eating contest.

09:45.501 --> 09:46.419
Hey.

09:47.253 --> 09:49.212
Are you two new?

09:49.213 --> 09:50.755
I see you've got lots of energy.

09:50.756 --> 09:52.340
JACK CASS
AKA KILL BABY

09:52.341 --> 09:54.175
28 YEARS OLD - SIXTH ATTEMPT AT EXAM

09:54.176 --> 09:56.469
What do you want, geezer?

09:56.470 --> 09:59.307
You'd better watch your mouth, brat.

10:00.141 --> 10:02.226
I've got a piece of advice for you.

10:02.768 --> 10:05.521
It's better to take the exam
on an empty stomach.

10:06.147 --> 10:09.524
Hunger sharpens the human senses.

10:09.525 --> 10:11.568
As always, he's bothering the newbies.

10:11.569 --> 10:13.737
What a <i>jackass.</i>

10:13.738 --> 10:16.782
Only one out of forty pass this exam.

10:17.366 --> 10:21.787
And the material changes every year,
so you don't know what to expect.

10:22.330 --> 10:25.749
You'd better be ready in your best state,
or you two will die.

10:25.750 --> 10:27.543
'Kay, whatever.

10:28.127 --> 10:29.045
<i>This is good soup.</i>

10:33.257 --> 10:36.301
Guys like you will be the first to die.

10:36.302 --> 10:38.220
I'll make sure to watch when you do!

10:39.722 --> 10:41.474
Your spaghetti wasn't even warm.

10:44.018 --> 10:45.144
Want me to kill him?

10:45.728 --> 10:48.731
<i>It's okay.
Killing him won't bring back my spaghetti.</i>

10:49.899 --> 10:50.733
<i>That's so mean...</i>

10:51.233 --> 10:55.904
<i>They must be new just like me,
nervous about the exam.</i>

10:55.905 --> 10:57.448
<i>He didn't have to...</i>

10:59.742 --> 11:03.245
<i>No, no. I'm in no position to pity them.</i>

11:03.746 --> 11:06.374
<i>Even a moment's distraction
could be the death of me.</i>

11:07.416 --> 11:10.252
<i>I'm going to pass this exam
and become an assassin.</i>

11:12.838 --> 11:15.091
<i>Oh, but I can't help
but feel sorry for them!</i>

11:15.716 --> 11:17.676
<i>Good luck, rookies!</i>

11:19.178 --> 11:22.181
Hello, JCC applicants,

11:22.723 --> 11:26.936
thank you very much for joining us today.

11:27.728 --> 11:30.897
My name is Mizuno.
If I could have your attention,

11:30.898 --> 11:34.693
I would like to explain
the rules of your exam before we arrive.

11:35.903 --> 11:40.323
Among the 360 applicants
aboard this flight,

11:40.324 --> 11:42.827
there are multiple
test examiners in disguise.

11:43.869 --> 11:45.370
Each examiner has

11:45.371 --> 11:49.083
special bullets with "JCC"
engraved on them.

11:49.667 --> 11:53.379
Your task is to identify the examiners
and steal a bullet.

11:53.921 --> 11:56.674
Examiner?
But they're professional assassins, right?

11:57.258 --> 11:58.717
We have to fight them?

11:59.385 --> 12:00.594
Question!

12:01.804 --> 12:04.722
Can I kill them when I steal the bullet?

12:04.723 --> 12:06.183
Yes, of course.

12:06.851 --> 12:08.978
If you can, that is.

12:12.648 --> 12:14.191
So, ladies and gentlemen,

12:16.694 --> 12:18.028
have a nice flight.

12:20.281 --> 12:21.907
It starts just like that?

12:32.626 --> 12:35.754
Poop, poop, gonna find some...

12:36.338 --> 12:37.380
An airplane!

12:37.381 --> 12:39.091
Bye-bye!

12:42.386 --> 12:45.180
Stop! I'm an applicant!

12:45.181 --> 12:46.765
You're lying!

12:49.518 --> 12:53.272
Your weapons have been assigned at random.

12:53.856 --> 12:57.026
Please utilize your weapons' features
as much as possible.

12:57.526 --> 12:58.986
Do you think I'm a joke?

12:59.695 --> 13:01.362
I demand you give me a new weapon!

13:01.363 --> 13:03.491
I can't get a fair fight with this!

13:04.325 --> 13:05.409
Huh?

13:13.167 --> 13:16.420
One must quickly adapt
to any situation, at any time.

13:17.046 --> 13:18.297
That's what hit men do.

13:34.897 --> 13:36.815
Drew another blank.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.276
Ew, gross.

13:43.072 --> 13:47.993
<i>The examiners are probably JCC instructors
or senior students working part-time.</i>

13:48.661 --> 13:52.706
<i>Which means they'd be among
those in their mid to late twenties.</i>

13:53.707 --> 13:57.628
<i>I'll study their movements
and narrow down my targets.</i>

13:58.879 --> 13:59.880
<i>This is stupid.</i>

14:01.715 --> 14:04.217
<i>They're so serious,
fighting from the get-go.</i>

14:04.218 --> 14:06.844
<i>I'm smart enough to wait
for them to kill each other.</i>

14:06.845 --> 14:09.890
<i>I'll just steal the bullet off
of whoever's left at the end.</i>

14:14.061 --> 14:15.020
I can't get him.

14:16.021 --> 14:17.313
Are you an examiner?

14:17.314 --> 14:18.232
<i>No...</i>

14:19.316 --> 14:20.234
'Kay, then.

14:23.863 --> 14:26.865
With all these people,
it's hard to hear what they're thinking.

14:26.866 --> 14:28.242
My head hurts.

14:29.451 --> 14:30.703
Hmm?

14:31.328 --> 14:33.037
Let's see here...

14:33.038 --> 14:35.207
How does this thing work?

14:36.333 --> 14:37.417
Lucky me.

14:37.418 --> 14:39.753
A wimp with a good weapon.

14:46.510 --> 14:49.012
I'm so sorry! I swear I didn't mean to!

14:49.013 --> 14:50.639
Please don't kill us!

14:56.020 --> 14:57.646
That's the guy from earlier.

15:01.275 --> 15:02.151
<i>A ball-point pen?!</i>

15:02.651 --> 15:04.527
<i>He drew a terrible weapon!</i>

15:04.528 --> 15:05.653
<i>Poor guy!</i>

15:05.654 --> 15:08.365
<i>That rookie is definitely going to die.</i>

15:14.455 --> 15:18.167
<i>Darn it! This is not the time to be
worrying about other people!</i>

15:21.378 --> 15:22.296
What?

15:26.884 --> 15:28.052
This is a nice pen.

15:29.178 --> 15:31.639
<i>What the... Who is this guy?</i>

15:33.682 --> 15:36.393
Man, that fatty's super strong.

15:37.019 --> 15:39.520
So that must mean... I'm sure of it!

15:39.521 --> 15:41.314
- He's an examiner!
- What?!

15:41.315 --> 15:42.690
- The fatty?
- Give me the bullet!

15:42.691 --> 15:43.901
What? Oh no!

15:49.949 --> 15:51.784
The bullet's mine!

16:09.843 --> 16:12.345
Um, sir? Thank you

16:12.346 --> 16:14.597
- for helping me.
- Got it.

16:14.598 --> 16:15.599
Huh?

16:16.266 --> 16:17.851
He's an examiner.

16:21.397 --> 16:24.857
Wow, I had no idea.

16:24.858 --> 16:26.735
And the way he fought bare-handed...

16:27.277 --> 16:29.362
It was like a veteran assassin.

16:29.363 --> 16:30.572
<i>I overdid it...</i>

16:33.117 --> 16:34.075
You...

16:34.076 --> 16:36.869
You're amazing! I'm absolutely impressed!

16:36.870 --> 16:39.373
As a fellow rookie,
you have my respect, sir!

16:40.749 --> 16:43.793
Watching you has been really inspiring.

16:43.794 --> 16:46.880
Yeah, all right then.
I gotta give it my all!

16:47.464 --> 16:48.465
I see.

16:49.049 --> 16:49.883
Good luck.

16:50.384 --> 16:51.218
Huh?

16:52.845 --> 16:54.013
I don't need three.

16:54.513 --> 16:55.806
What?!

16:56.807 --> 16:59.058
<i>I wonder where he went.</i>

16:59.059 --> 17:02.312
No, you mustn't! I can't accept this!

17:05.524 --> 17:08.651
You see, I have a role model.

17:08.652 --> 17:11.447
And I don't think
that person would accept the bullet.

17:11.989 --> 17:14.450
I mean, it's not like
I'm anything like them...

17:15.534 --> 17:17.201
I'm so puny.

17:17.202 --> 17:20.121
I've been told I'd be better off
doing chores than hits.

17:20.122 --> 17:21.873
That's what my parents would say.

17:21.874 --> 17:25.127
You'll never know until you try.

17:27.755 --> 17:31.133
You're right. You just proved to me
that body size doesn't matter!

17:32.885 --> 17:36.096
Oh no, sorry!
That's not what I meant! I'm so sorry!

17:40.434 --> 17:42.477
Come on, you're so weak.

17:42.478 --> 17:46.023
Those who can't do hits,
teach at the JCC, huh?

17:46.523 --> 17:48.400
This is too easy.

17:49.026 --> 17:52.153
Applicant number four, Mafuyu Seba...

17:52.154 --> 17:53.572
You're not too bad.

17:55.407 --> 17:58.243
I'm allowed to kill you for this, right?

17:58.744 --> 18:00.871
That's what you said.

18:05.793 --> 18:06.627
How annoying.

18:07.503 --> 18:09.337
Stay outta my way, geezer.

18:09.338 --> 18:12.423
Huh? Who you calling a geezer?

18:12.424 --> 18:14.842
I'm only 21!

18:14.843 --> 18:19.348
Well, I'm 14, so 21 is a geezer, for sure.

18:25.479 --> 18:26.313
Shit!

18:35.364 --> 18:37.699
<i>He's used to combat.</i>

18:38.909 --> 18:39.867
What?

18:39.868 --> 18:41.245
Ugh, that sucks!

18:42.037 --> 18:44.580
That's so disgusting!

18:44.581 --> 18:47.708
That is so not cool.
I could report you for harassment.

18:47.709 --> 18:49.544
You knew what you were getting into!

18:49.545 --> 18:51.213
What are you, a germaphobe?!

18:52.965 --> 18:56.592
It's not like I wanted to take
the Transfer Exam.

18:56.593 --> 19:01.013
My stupid big brother gave me the flu
on the day of the General Admissions Exam.

19:01.014 --> 19:04.851
I bet everyone's already made
groups and cliques... This sucks.

19:04.852 --> 19:08.230
<i>What's with this entitled germaphobe?</i>

19:09.690 --> 19:12.024
Like, I seriously don't want to get dirty.

19:12.025 --> 19:13.735
I really hate it.

19:14.361 --> 19:16.738
I need to keep clean...

19:21.076 --> 19:24.121
So I make sure I don't get my hands dirty.

19:27.541 --> 19:28.667
<i>A hidden weapon!</i>

19:31.628 --> 19:32.629
<i>He's so fast!</i>

19:34.590 --> 19:35.424
That was close.

19:59.573 --> 20:00.782
<i>Little punk!</i>

20:01.533 --> 20:02.409
Die!

20:10.083 --> 20:11.168
<i>I gotta get better.</i>

20:11.752 --> 20:13.921
<i>I can't keep weighing down Mr. Sakamoto.</i>

20:18.133 --> 20:19.301
<i>What was that?</i>

20:19.801 --> 20:21.637
<i>How did he know all of my moves?</i>

20:27.017 --> 20:28.143
Sorry, kid.

20:29.394 --> 20:30.395
There's someone

20:31.772 --> 20:33.941
I need to catch up to, fast.

22:08.035 --> 22:09.410
ONE YEAR AGO

22:09.411 --> 22:10.537
Mr. Uda,

22:11.413 --> 22:13.832
I got these for you.

22:17.419 --> 22:19.962
A beginner's guide for spies,
some supplements,

22:19.963 --> 22:22.257
and a few canned foods that looked good.

22:23.050 --> 22:24.592
Thank you, Mr. Kashima.

22:24.593 --> 22:25.510
MINERALS - MACKEREL

22:26.470 --> 22:27.512
This is from me.

22:31.683 --> 22:33.977
I drew you with zinnia flowers.

22:34.519 --> 22:36.438
Look up the meaning
of the flower later, okay?

22:37.898 --> 22:40.358
<i>Boss is getting better at drawing.</i>

22:41.109 --> 22:42.486
I appreciate it.

22:45.405 --> 22:46.865
Okay then, I'm going.

22:50.368 --> 22:53.162
Gaku, Uda's leaving.

22:53.163 --> 22:55.539
Come and see him off.

22:55.540 --> 22:56.750
Right.

22:57.250 --> 22:59.002
He'll be back soon, anyway.

23:00.212 --> 23:02.922
Gaku, where are your manners?

23:02.923 --> 23:04.591
It's okay, Mr. Kashima.

23:06.802 --> 23:09.513
Let's go to karaoke when I'm back, Gaku.

23:10.514 --> 23:11.848
Good luck, man.

23:22.776 --> 23:24.111
<i>I'm bored.</i>

23:24.861 --> 23:25.862
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
